                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 3,
                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "I joined Frank McCaffrey on Inside Valley Politics to warn South Texas about the consequences of letting the Affordable Care Act's tax credits expire.\n\nWithout these tax credits, premiums will surge and more people will go uninsured. TX-34 already has one of the highest uninsured rates in the nation, which is why I'll continue to fight to extend these credits. South Texans deserve access to high quality, affordable health care.",
